    "rationale": "Amorphous silicon. There is no canonical a-Si: n and k depend on the deposition. Karaman 2025 is a 100-nm a-Si film on fused silica at 20 C, a typical metasurface platform, so it is a reasonable default -- NOT a claim about any particular deposition. Replace it with ellipsometry of the real film before a number goes in a report. CAUTION: this entry's k is exactly 0 above 856 nm, which is the ellipsometry's detection floor and not physics -- real a-Si keeps a sub-gap Urbach/dangling-bond tail of order 1e-4. Do not read a loss-free 1550 nm a-Si mirror off this table; absorption there is a measurement, not a database lookup."
